tests:
  unit:
    count: 6
    covers: "6 new test functions, table-driven rather than one-case-per-fn, over the three files this WU changed. xtask/src/doc.rs (+2): new_surface - a @tier file under ui/src/components/ fires, an untiered collection file does not, a non-test .tsx directly under ui/src/ fires, its .test.tsx does not, a .ts module does not, a Rust file does not; and roster_at over a revision rather than the working tree. xtask/src/gate.rs (+2): over real temp repos - the trigger sees an added component and not its test, its .ts sibling or an untouched component, and an edit and a deletion add no surface; then one red per way a citation breaks (silence on v3, silence on v2 routed to 9·design-schema, an empty list, an unresolvable path, a mismatched blob, a pin too short, a doc that is not a design, an unarchived run) and one green when it all holds; plus components·unbuilt's four answers - unbuilt reds, a blank-reason drop still reds, a drop with a reason greens and is billed as a waiver, a built component owes nothing. xtask/src/notes.rs (+2): absent and empty design.implements parse differently and stay that way, and a drop parses as path + reason with a blank reason being no drop. Totals at this tip: 196 xtask lib tests, all green"
  integration:
    count: 3
    covers: "xtask/tests/dod_gate.rs 66 -> 69, the bounded contract driven through the real binary against temp trees. verify-dod wu reds a tip whose diff adds a @tier component and whose note names no design, and the red names the surface; greens on the same tip with a resolvable citation; and reds a STALE citation - the blob is compared against the tip, not the working tree, so a design edited after the note was written cannot pass. verify-dod epic reds a range that added a component design with no roster entry, stays red with a reasonless drop, greens and bills the reason as a waiver, and needs no record at all once the component lands. Totals at this tip: 69 dod_gate tests, all green"
  e2e:
    count: 2
    covers: "NOT WAIVED - this WU's whole exercise, and the epic level the plan refused to defer. xtask/tests/e2e_design_flow.rs 2 -> 4 (--features design-e2e, out of the default suite as the existing flow e2e is): a_build_that_adds_a_surface_cites_the_design_it_read_or_the_merge_refuses_it and a_design_nobody_built_refuses_the_epic_merge_until_the_drop_is_recorded. Six cases over real git through the real merge hook - 8 merges, 5 refused and 3 landed. Each red is bound to its own message (cites no design / cites ... at blob / is a design artifact the design section does not name / components·unbuilt) rather than to a check name, because 9·design is a prefix of 9·design-schema and a bare substring assertion would pass on the wrong red"
